; ..\_01_BSW\Src\Os\Os_ServiceFunction.c	  1769   \DESCRIPTION    Os_ThreadSetCurrentApplication is called with a PrevApplication which is derived from a
; ..\_01_BSW\Src\Os\Os_ServiceFunction.c	  1770                   ServiceCall. The ServiceCall is passed as argument to the caller. The correctness of the caller
; ..\_01_BSW\Src\Os\Os_ServiceFunction.c	  1771                   argument is ensured by precondition. PrevApplication is initialized in Os_ServicePrologue. Precondition
; ..\_01_BSW\Src\Os\Os_ServiceFunction.c	  1772                   ensures that Os_ServicePrologue is called before. The compliance of the preconditions is check during
; ..\_01_BSW\Src\Os\Os_ServiceFunction.c	  1773                   review.
; ..\_01_BSW\Src\Os\Os_ServiceFunction.c	  1774   \COUNTERMEASURE \M [CM_OS_SF_OWNERAPPLICATION_M]
