; ..\_01_BSW\Src\Os\Os_ServiceFunction.c	  1777   \DESCRIPTION    Os_MpSwitch is called with a MpAccessRights object and a PrevMpAccessRights object.
; ..\_01_BSW\Src\Os\Os_ServiceFunction.c	  1778                   The MpAccessRights object is derived from a Service object. The PrevMpAccessRights is initialized with
; ..\_01_BSW\Src\Os\Os_ServiceFunction.c	  1779                   the return value of Os_ThreadGetMpAccessRights. The PrevMpAccessRights object is derived
; ..\_01_BSW\Src\Os\Os_ServiceFunction.c	  1780                   from a ServiceCall object. Service and ServiceCall are passed as argument to the caller.
; ..\_01_BSW\Src\Os\Os_ServiceFunction.c	  1781                   The correctness of the caller arguments is ensured by precondition. The compliance of the precondition
; ..\_01_BSW\Src\Os\Os_ServiceFunction.c	  1782                   is check during review.
; ..\_01_BSW\Src\Os\Os_ServiceFunction.c	  1783   \COUNTERMEASURE \M [CM_OS_SF_MPACCESSRIGHTS_M]
